{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-is:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-is:f4084716095b118f69f49d05f351ba7b01ed78d683e7fe5f1a264b63ac747dca","timestamp":"2026-11-08T16:42:40Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.3r.linker.w0","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-is","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-is","title":"Close-outcome letter aliases (x → !, s → *) in Bob Mac Capture","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-08T16:42:40Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.3r.linker.w0","updated_at":"2026-11-08T16:42:40Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"In the Bob Mac Capture editor, a plain lowercase `x` typed where a close selection accepts an outcome marker becomes `!`, and a plain lowercase `s` becomes `*`. Examples: `xx` → `x!`, `xs` → `x*`, `x1s` → `x1*`, `x=1=s` → `x=1=*`, and `@r:id=xx` → `@r:id=x!`. Bob's `capture-rewrite` alone decides where the alias fires. `bob capture`, `capture-parse`, paste, and CLI text keep the letters. Typing speed never changes the outcome: keys typed before Bob answers are held and replayed, and a fast Return never files the literal draft.","design":"plan:202611/close_outcome_x_s_typing_aliases.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/close_outcome_x_s_typing_aliases.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
